#====================================================================
# DRAFT-gnustep-gui-ohos-autoconf-cross-probe
# OHOS CI must not execute unsigned autoconf conftest probes
#
# 本条目为 draft，不预占正式 E 编号，禁止直接 promote。
# 触发事件: gnustep-gui 0.32.0 HarmonyOS PC 适配（PR #7095 CI #34102）
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-gnustep-gui-ohos-autoconf-cross-probe
trigger_tool:           configure|autoconf|conan
phase:                  configure
error_signature:        checking whether we are cross compiling.*cannot run C compiled programs|If you meant to cross compile, use '--host'|cannot run C compiled programs

severity:               2
category:               autotools|ohos|configure|cross-compiling|xpm
match_keywords:         autoconf, configure, conftest, a.out, cross_compiling, --build,
                         --host, --target, OHOS, HarmonyOS, unsigned executable

title:                  Force OHOS autoconf configure into cross mode before unsigned conftest probes run
root_cause: >
  On HarmonyOS CI, the compiler can produce a temporary C executable, but autoconf native
  mode then tries to run conftest/a.out. The temporary executable is outside the normal
  signed package/install path and can be rejected by the worker runtime domain. When Conan
  emits equal build and host triplets such as aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos, autoconf keeps
  cross_compiling=no and fails at the execution probe.
affected_scope: >
  gnustep-gui and similar autotools recipes on OHOS where generated build/host triplets are
  equal and configure reaches a run-time compiler probe before the actual package build.
verification_cmd: >
  Inspect the configure command in CI; it should contain --build=<cpu>-unknown-linux-gnu,
  --host=<cpu>-unknown-linux-ohos, --target=<cpu>-unknown-linux-ohos, and
  ac_cv_prog_cc_works=yes exactly once after filtering generated triplets.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           filter-generated-triplets-and-force-autoconf-cross-mode
rec_description: >
  In the OHOS recipe path, filter generated --build/--host/--target values from the final
  configure argument string, then invoke configure with build set to a GNU/Linux triplet and
  host/target set to the OHOS triplet for the same CPU. Add ac_cv_prog_cc_works=yes as a
  guard for compiler-work probes, but keep the behavior scoped to OHOS.
rec_command: >
  configure --build=<cpu>-unknown-linux-gnu --host=<cpu>-unknown-linux-ohos
  --target=<cpu>-unknown-linux-ohos ac_cv_prog_cc_works=yes
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-configure-wrapper

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-configure-cache-vars-only-after-triplets-are-fixed
fallback_description: >
  If configure has additional AC_RUN_IFELSE probes, cache only the specific probe variables
  after build/host triplets already force cross_compiling=yes. Do not globally disable large
  feature sets to bypass the probe.
fallback_command:       add targeted ac_cv_* cache values beside the OHOS configure args
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          targeted-configure-cache

forbid_1_pattern:       duplicate --build=.*--build=|duplicate --host=.*--host=
forbid_1_reason:        Duplicate triplets make configure parsing order ambiguous in CI logs and reviews.
forbid_1_consequence:   The recipe can still run native probes or become difficult to audit.

forbid_2_pattern:       disable AppKit|--without-gui|skip GNUstep GUI build
forbid_2_reason:        The failure is a configure probe/runtime policy issue, not an AppKit feature issue.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package would no longer validate the intended gnustep-gui surface.

principles:             P016
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

